+---
+"@gpuix/solid": patch
+---
+
+Close a live macOS window from resetRender so process exit does not drop it during thread-local teardown.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index bdcc74d..c0ffee1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -75,6 +75,11 @@ query still require explicit JS registration but cannot prove native availability.
 Initialize the renderer before mounting; use the same installed addon for both
 the host and framework. Custom props, events and instance lifetimes then use the
 normal Solid mutation path, including reactive updates and unmount/remount.
+
+`resetRender()` unmounts the Solid root and closes a live macOS window before
+the process exits. GPUI records that close in a profiler thread-local. Dropping
+an open window during process-exit thread-local teardown panics. Call
+`resetRender()` or `closeWindow()` before `process.exit`.
 
 ## Multiple native windows on macOS
 
